      "devanagari": "धूम्राक्षः परमामर्षी सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः |\nअकम्पनः प्रहस्तश्च कुम्भकर्णस्त्तथैव च\nएते महाबला वीरा राक्षसा युद्धकाङिक्षणः |\nजेतारः परसैन्यानां परैर्नित्यापराजिताः\nससैन्यास्ते हता वीरा रामेणाक्लिष्टकर्मणा |\nराक्षसाः सुमहाकाया नानाशस्त्रविशारदाः\nअन्ये च बहवः शूरा महात्मानो निपातिताः |",
      "iast": "dhūmrākṣaḥ paramāmarṣī sarvaśastrabhṛtāṃ varaḥ |\nakampanaḥ prahastaśca kumbhakarṇasttathaiva ca\nete mahābalā vīrā rākṣasā yuddhakāṇ^ikṣaṇaḥ |\njetāraḥ parasainyānāṃ parairnityāparājitāḥ\nsasainyāste hatā vīrā rāmeṇākliṣṭakarmaṇā |\nrākṣasāḥ sumahākāyā nānāśastraviśāradāḥ\nanye ca bahavaḥ śūrā mahātmāno nipātitāḥ |",
      "translation": "\"Dhumraksha, who was greatly impatient Akampana who was excellent among all wielders of weapons, Prahasta and Kumbhakarna were killed by Rama, who was unwearied in battle. The mighty and valiant demons longing for battle, who conquer the adversaries, who was never defeated in battle by the enemies they along with their enemies were killed. Many other mighty warriors.",
